DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("7-((((x)^2))^2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^((sin(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-9, -6, -4, -3, 1, 8} - {-10, -6, 1})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-10, -6, 1} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -6, -4, -3, 1, 8}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-8, -3, 1, 7, 8} U ({-10, -6, 1} U (({-9, -6, -4, -3, 1, 8}))))))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(({-10, -6, 1})) U {-9, -6, -4, -3, 1, 8} U {-8, -3, 1, 7, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(((4, infinity)) - {-1, 0, 1, 4, 9})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(4, infinity) U (4, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, infinity)) U {-1, 0, 1, 4, 9}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`3+16-8*14`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>-93,width=>4}
---

[`19+16*9`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>163,width=>4}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-3, 3, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 3\}`]
- [`C = \{-1, 0, 1, 4, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B) - C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup B \cap B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -3, 1, 7, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -6, 1\}`]
- [`C = \{-9, -6, -4, -3, 1, 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`C - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cap C \cap ((A \cup (B \cup ((C))))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`((B)) \cup C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, 8, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 2, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, 0, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, 2, 6>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 8, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 8, 3>") . Compute("<-3, 0, 5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, 8, 3>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 6, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 9, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, 6, -7>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 9, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 9, 4>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 6, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
